## Findings
- At 847x996, the Hero section tagline "One Library. Every Connector on Earth." is overlapping with "Trusted by the fastest growing businesses globally".
- The CTA buttons "Get Started" and "Connectors" are overlapping with the logos in the trust band.
- **Cause**: The "Logo Pull-up" mentioned in the planner response involved increasing the negative margin on the trust band. At this specific viewport height (996px), this negative margin is too aggressive, pulling the trust band too far up and causing it to overlap with the Hero section content.
- The Hero section's `min-height` was also reduced, which further exacerbated the overlap because the content within the Hero section has less space before the trust band starts.
- The specific CSS property is `margin-top` (with a negative value) on the trust band section container.

## Summary
The overlap is confirmed at the specified resolution. The combination of a reduced `min-height` on the hero section and an increased negative `margin-top` on the subsequent "trust band" section is causing the content of both sections to clash visually.
